diff --git a/packages/frai-core/README.md b/packages/frai-core/README.md
index ce5733b..1e40211 100644
--- a/packages/frai-core/README.md
+++ b/packages/frai-core/README.md
@@ -181,6 +181,41 @@ await fs.writeFile('ai-context.txt', aiContext);
 
 Because `frai-core` is a regular ESM package, you can import only the modules you need and embed FRAI capabilities inside automation pipelines, CI jobs, or custom products.
 
+### Evaluation with Thresholds
+
+Use `Eval.generateReport` with thresholds to gate CI on metric scores:
+
+```ts
+import { Eval } from 'frai-core';
+
+const dataset = Eval.loadDataset({
+  outputsPath: './outputs.json',
+  referencesPath: './references.json'
+});
+
+const evaluations = Eval.runEvaluations({
+  outputs: dataset.outputs,
+  references: dataset.references
+});
+
+const report = Eval.generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  outputsPath: dataset.outputsPath,
+  referencesPath: dataset.referencesPath,
+  thresholds: {
+    exact_match: 0.9,
+    toxicity: 0.95
+  }
+});
+
+// report.passed indicates whether all thresholds were met
+if (report.passed === false) {
+  process.exit(1); // Fail CI
+}
+```
+
+Thresholds accept a `{ metric_id: minimum_score }` object. A metric with no score (null) fails its threshold. The report includes a `thresholds` array with pass/fail results for each.
+
 ---
 
 ## Local Development
